{\Huge \textbf{Abstract}}\\
\vspace{15mm}
This report documents the work completed during a 3-ECTS internship, focused on the implementation and study of data-driven Model Predictive Control (MPC) with stability and robustness guarantees. Based on the foundational work by  J. Berberich, J. Kohler, M. A. Muller, and F. Allgower, “Data-Driven Model Predictive Control with
Stability and Robustness Guarantees”, the internship aimed at deepening understanding of behavioral systems theory and its application to MPC through hands-on coding in Python using CasADi. No original research was conducted; instead, the internship focused on reproducing and understanding the theoretical and algorithmic components of the cited work.
\end{center}
